    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 28 May 2019, the Minister of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship introduced Bill C-99, Act to amend the Citizenship Act, in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.   &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-99 amends the Citizenship Act to include, in the Oath or Affirmation of Citizenship, a solemn promise to respect the Aboriginal and treaty rights of First Nations, Inuit and Métis peoples.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>&lt;div&gt;Le Service d'information et de recherche parlementaires de la Bibliothèque du Parlement rédige actuellement le résumé législatif de ce projet de loi.  Entre-temps, le Service met à votre disposition le sommaire suivant.  &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le 28 mai 2019, le Ministre de l'Immigration, des Réfugiés et de la Citoyenneté a déposé le projet de loi C-99, Loi modifiant la Loi sur la citoyenneté à la Chambre des communes en première lecture.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Le projet de loi C-99 modifie la Loi sur la citoyenneté afin d'inclure une promesse solennelle de respecter les droits — ancestraux ou issus de traités — des Premières Nations, des Inuits et des Métis dans le serment de citoyenneté et l'affirmation solennelle.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>&lt;div&gt;A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;On 28 May 2019, the Minister of Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship introduced Bill C-99, Act to amend the Citizenship Act, in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.   &lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Bill C-99 amends the Citizenship Act to include, in the Oath or Affirmation of Citizenship, a solemn promise to respect the Aboriginal and treaty rights of First Nations, Inuit and Métis peoples.&lt;/div&gt;</ShortLegislativeSummary>
